# open62541-qnx change: udp-empty-datagram
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Do not close a UDP socket because of an empty datagram
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix_udp.c
# test: pubsub.unicast.empty_datagram
#
# A UDP datagram without payload is a valid datagram, and recvfrom() returns
# 0 for it. The code takes every result <= 0 except EINTR as the end of the
# socket and closes it. A PubSub connection reopens its receive socket only if
# it has received a message before; a subscriber that gets an empty datagram
# before its first message stays without a socket. Anybody who can reach the
# port can send that datagram.
#
# The same branch also closes the socket after EAGAIN, which a wake-up without
# a readable datagram produces.
#
@@ hunk
